{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d62c9e17ed58a2d1","name":"TIE Interceptor","source":{"id":"source:reference-d62c9e17ed58a2d1","title":"TIE Interceptor","revision":18563,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:19:41Z","sha256":"ae5986c405ae0315d172f8870cc5a1456ac4a13a225c7364c7277f07730f52f7","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18563","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=TIE%20Interceptor&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d62c9e17ed58a2d1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Books: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The TIE Interceptor was designed specifically to counteract the Rebel ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:3633fb1b1140ece1"},". To increase speed and firepower, the designers at Sienar gave it large engines, more powerful energy converters, and a package of four Fire-Linked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"},". Although put into production before the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},", these Starfighters weren't in general use until just before the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endor"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["After the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},", Imperial Naval commanders demanded a Starfighter that could counter the speed and firepower of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing_Starfighters"}," that ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Rebel Alliance"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Rebel_Alliance","referenceId":"reference:52c543ff6d31425c"}," had employed. The TIE Interceptor, which incorporated several of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Advanced"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Advanced","referenceId":"reference:9dc439f5ab09e14f"}," prototype's features, was the ultimate result. Prototypes similar to the initial interceptor design had undergone testing prior to the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},", but these had seen little action outside Sienar's test yards.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["It was only a short time later that the final TIE Interceptor design was integrated into existing Starfighter squadrons. The Imperial Navy's eventual plan was to replace all standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"}," with TIE Interceptors. This lofty goal was never quite met, with Interceptors representing only twenty percent of all TIEs by the time the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Endor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Endor"}," took place. As the number of TIE Interceptors in the Imperial Navy increased, it became standard procedure to include at least one squadron of TIE Interceptors aboard each ",{"tag":"a","children":["Star Destroyer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Star_Destroyer"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The TIE Interceptor is a consumable dogfighter, possessed of increased speed and maneuverability when compared to the standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},". Not only is the Interceptor faster and more agile than the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighter","referenceId":"reference:726e84ae35ac767c"},", it also incorporates four Fire-Linked ",{"tag":"a","children":["Laser Cannons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Laser_Cannons"}," mounted on the tips of it's bent, dagger-shaped solar arrays. The solar arrays themselves featured a horizontal notch that improves pilot visibility on both sides. Although it lacks shields, armor, and life support, the TIE Interceptor has proven to be more than a match for the ",{"tag":"a","children":["X-Wing Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/X-Wing_Starfighter","referenceId":"reference:3633fb1b1140ece1"},". Interceptor tactics are nearly identical to those utilized by standard ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Fighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Fighters"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Skilled)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["TIE Interceptor Statistics (CL 8)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 18 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 24; +3 Armor, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.mirahez